  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nThere is not much to write home about in the forecast for the next \nseveral days. The upper level ridge currently centered over the four \ncorners will continue to remain nearly stationary through at least \nthe first half of next week. An upper level trough moving onshore on \nthe west coast will weaken the ridge and shift it to the \nsoutheastern US starting around mid-week next week. Despite the \nweakening ridge, temperatures will remain nearly identical day to \nday slightly above seasonal averages. Because of the movement of the \nridge, models have backed off a bit on mid-week precipitation \nchances. The ridge is now expected to intensify more late week \npossibly bringing more monsoonal like convection to the area.",
